{
  "steps": [
    {
      "npc": "Welcome to the Laughing Miner pub, human traveller."
    },
    {
      "type": "choice",
      "options": [
        {
          "text": "Who is that man walking around outside?",
          "steps": [
            {
              "player": "Who is that man walking around outside?"
            },
            {
              "npc": "What man?"
            },
            {
              "player": "I mean the dwarf, the one with the sign."
            },
            {
              "npc": "Oh, him. Yes, we employ him to advertise our pub, he's the cheapest labour we could find. We don't have a lot of money to spare you know, we pay him in beer."
            },
            {
              "player": "But what's wrong with him?"
            },
            {
              "npc": "Well, he's drunk isn't he?"
            },
            {
              "npc": "I told you, he's cheap. He couldn't get any other work since the Red Axe fired him. Been drinking ever since."
            },
            {
              "player": "How did that happen?"
            },
            {
              "npc": "I'm not quite sure, I think he kept wearing the wrong coloured cap all the time. They don't much like it if you don't wear your red uniform into work."
            },
            {
              "player": "They fired him for that??"
            },
            {
              "npc": "The Red Axe will fire you for just about anything if they want to."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "I'd like a beer please.",
          "steps": [
